title: 'Asset Hub Westend: validators collate on Bulletin Westend'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Asset Hub Westend sends the validator set of every era to Bulletin Westend, as it does to
    People, and accepts Bulletin's reports of authored blocks for era points.

    One list of parachain IDs, `ValidatorCollatorChains`, names the chains that receive the
    validator set, report their authored blocks and get explicit unpaid execution at the barrier.
    The set is sent as an unpaid `Transact` of `set_validators` with the `Xcm` origin kind. Asset
    Hub encodes the call with the same pallet index of `ValidatorCollators` on every receiving
    chain. The Bulletin Westend runtime is built outside this repository, so it must keep that
    index.
crates:
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: testnet-parachains-constants
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-zombienet-sdk-tests
  bump: none
